{"id": 41, "ts": 1779485926.9291255, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "Based on the consolidated evidence, I see Candidate\u202fC as the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role. C demonstrates strong stress resilience (calm in crisis), solid technical competence (understands complex technology), high decision quality (quick, correct decisions), and reliability (100\u202f% reliable) while also fostering a positive crew atmosphere. The primary concerns are C\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric demeanor, and limited willingness for further education, which could affect crew cooperation and adaptability. Compared with Candidate\u202fB, whose memory weakness and hostile remarks raise serious attention\u2011accuracy and teamwork risks, and Candidate\u202fA and D, whose openness and temperament issues are more pronounced, C\u2019s strengths outweigh the noted gaps. I propose we provisionally advance Candidate\u202fC, while arranging a reference check focused on communication style and willingness to develop further.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
