{"id": 64, "ts": 1779486077.6524777, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "Having reviewed the dossier and all interview observations, the panel now has a complete picture of each candidate\u2019s strengths and gaps. Candidate\u202fC demonstrates the highest overall fit: 100\u202f% operational reliability, a consistently positive crew atmosphere, quick and correct decision\u2011making, calmness in crises, and solid technical understanding. The only remaining uncertainty concerns his egocentric attitude and willingness to accept feedback, but no evidence suggests this has impaired his teamwork in practice.\nCandidate\u202fD, while strong in problem\u2011solving, responsibility, and concentration, lacks any observed evidence of stress resilience or leadership under high\u2011pressure cockpit scenarios\u2014critical criteria for long\u2011distance flights. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress handling is offset by clear interpersonal deficiencies (nasty remarks, grumpiness) that jeopardize crew cooperation. Candidate\u202fA\u2019s leadership potential is undermined by disorganization and resistance to criticism.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC remains the most suitable choice for the long\u2011distance pilot role, provided we monitor his feedback orientation during onboarding.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
